## 3. Exploring a DataFrame

```python
df.head()        # first 5 rows
df.head(10)      # first 10 rows
df.info()        # column names, data types, non-null counts
df.describe()    # summary stats for numeric columns only
df.shape         # (number of rows, number of columns) — no parentheses, it's an attribute
df.columns       # list of column names
```

